{"term":"дупло","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"duplo","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":58,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for the vagina, derived from the Russian word for a hollow in a tree or wall, emphasizing its concave shape.","english_term":"hole","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Literal meaning is 'tree hollow' or 'cavity'; one of several hollow-themed slang terms for vagina in Russian; less common than пизда but understood by most adults."}
{"term":"коробочка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"korobochka","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":30,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Euphemistic slang for the vagina, literally 'little box,' playing on the container metaphor common across many languages.","english_term":"box","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Diminutive of коробка (box); relatively mild and used playfully rather than crudely; the box metaphor parallels English slang usage."}
{"term":"ракушка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"rakushka","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":30,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":50,"recognition_pct_peak":50,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang for the vagina, literally 'seashell' or 'clam shell,' evoking the shape of the external female genitalia.","english_term":"clam","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The seashell metaphor parallels English slang 'clam'; used in casual or playful registers rather than overtly coarse ones."}
{"term":"лялька","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"lyal'ka","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":40,"recognition_pct_peak":40,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Childish or playful euphemism for the vagina, from a dialectal word for 'doll' or 'toy'; used especially when speaking to or about young children.","english_term":"girly parts","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"More common in southern Russian and Ukrainian-influenced speech; low crudeness but clearly sexual in context; often used by parents with small children."}
{"term":"мандавошки","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"mandavoshki","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"pubic_lice","is_novel_concept":true,"register":"slang_crude","crude":78,"technical":10,"recognition_pct_current":78,"recognition_pct_peak":78,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for pubic lice, formed from манда (vulgar word for vulva/vagina) plus вошки (lice); grouped in vaginal vocabulary because of its morphological root.","english_term":"crabs","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"The word itself means 'pubic lice,' not 'vagina'; its high crudeness rating derives from the root манда, itself a mat-adjacent obscenity for the vulva; proposed new slug: pubic_lice."}
{"term":"пиздёнка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"pizdyonka","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":88,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Diminutive form of пизда used as crude slang for the vagina; the diminutive suffix slightly reduces force but keeps it firmly in the mat register.","english_term":"cunt","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Diminutive of пизда; the -ёнка suffix suggests smallness or youth; sometimes carries a condescending or sexualizing diminutive tone rather than simple size reference."}
{"term":"пизда","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"pizda","category":"organs","subcategory":"vagina","concept":"vagina","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":98,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The primary and harshest Russian obscenity for the vagina; a mat-level obscenity comparable in severity to 'cunt' in American English, though even more culturally taboo in most Russian contexts.","english_term":"cunt","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"One of the four canonical Russian mat words (alongside хуй, ебать, блядь); used as a general intensifier and in many fixed expressions beyond its anatomical meaning; cognate with Ukrainian піzда and other Slavic forms."}
{"term":"клитор","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"klitor","category":"organs","subcategory":"clitoris","concept":"clitoris","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":10,"technical":88,"recognition_pct_current":94,"recognition_pct_peak":94,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard clinical and everyday Russian term for the clitoris, a direct loanword from Greek/Latin via European medical terminology.","english_term":"clitoris","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Used in both medical contexts and ordinary speech; no inherent vulgar connotation though the subject matter may cause social embarrassment in conservative settings."}
{"term":"половой бугорок","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"polovoy bugorok","category":"organs","subcategory":"clitoris","concept":"clitoris","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":5,"technical":90,"recognition_pct_current":30,"recognition_pct_peak":30,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Clinical anatomical term for the clitoris, literally 'genital tubercle' or 'sexual bump'; used primarily in medical and embryological contexts.","english_term":"clitoral tubercle","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Половой = sexual/genital (from пол = sex/gender); бугорок = small mound or tubercle; most common in embryological and developmental anatomy contexts where the homology with the glans penis is being described."}
{"term":"кнопка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"knopka","category":"organs","subcategory":"clitoris","concept":"clitoris","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":20,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":72,"recognition_pct_peak":72,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang for the clitoris, literally 'button,' a cross-linguistic metaphor based on its small size and the way it is stimulated.","english_term":"button","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"The button metaphor for the clitoris appears in many languages; playful rather than crude; кнопка is also the ordinary Russian word for a button or thumbtack, so context disambiguates."}
{"term":"бугорок","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"bugorok","category":"organs","subcategory":"clitoris","concept":"clitoris","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":18,"recognition_pct_current":55,"recognition_pct_peak":55,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Mild slang for the clitoris, literally 'little mound' or 'small bump'; descriptive rather than crude, functioning as a non-offensive circumlocution.","english_term":"little mound","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Shares the root of the clinical term половой бугорок but used in casual rather than strictly medical speech; understood primarily by adults familiar with the anatomy."}
{"term":"кнопочка","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"knopochka","category":"organs","subcategory":"clitoris","concept":"clitoris","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":15,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":65,"recognition_pct_peak":65,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Affectionate diminutive slang for the clitoris, literally 'tiny button'; the diminutive suffix adds endearment, typically used in intimate or playful contexts.","english_term":"little button","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Diminutive of кнопка; the -очка suffix marks it as affectionate or tender; lower crudeness than кнопка because the diminutive frames it as something precious rather than merely colloquial."}
{"term":"грудь","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"grud'","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breast","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":5,"technical":55,"recognition_pct_current":99,"recognition_pct_peak":99,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard neutral Russian word for breast or chest; the default everyday term for the female breast used in speech, literature, and semi-clinical contexts.","english_term":"breast","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Грудь means both 'chest' (anatomical region) and 'breast' (mammary organ); context disambiguates; not crude and used freely in polite company; applies to both male and female anatomy."}
{"term":"молочные железы","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"molochnye zhelezy","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breast","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":0,"technical":95,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard clinical Russian term for mammary glands, literally 'milk glands'; used in medical, scientific, and educational contexts.","english_term":"mammary glands","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Plural; молочные = milky/milk (from молоко); железы = glands; purely clinical, rarely used outside medical or health education contexts; recognized by most educated adults."}
{"term":"грудная железа","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"grudnaya zheleza","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breast","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":0,"technical":90,"recognition_pct_current":58,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Clinical anatomical term for a single mammary gland, literally 'chest gland'; less common than the plural молочные железы but appears in medical texts.","english_term":"mammary gland","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Singular form; грудная = of the chest/breast (from грудь); железа = gland; slightly less common in practice than молочные железы; both terms appear in medical literature."}
{"term":"сосок","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"sosok","category":"organs","subcategory":"nipple","concept":"nipple","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":15,"technical":72,"recognition_pct_current":97,"recognition_pct_peak":97,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The standard Russian term for nipple, used in both clinical and everyday speech; derived from the verb сосать (to suck), referencing the breastfeeding function.","english_term":"nipple","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"From сосать = to suck; mild crudeness arises from the erogenous nature of the organ rather than the word itself; universally known and used freely in medical and everyday speech."}
{"term":"ареола","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"areola","category":"organs","subcategory":"areola","concept":"areola","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"clinical","crude":0,"technical":92,"recognition_pct_current":60,"recognition_pct_peak":60,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Clinical term for the areola, the pigmented ring surrounding the nipple; a direct loanword from Latin areola via European medical terminology.","english_term":"areola","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Direct cognate with English 'areola'; purely clinical and rarely encountered outside medical or detailed anatomical contexts; recognition is growing through online health education."}
{"term":"сиськи","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"sis'ki","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":70,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":98,"recognition_pct_peak":98,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"The most widespread crude slang for female breasts in Russian; extremely common in informal speech, humor, internet culture, and vulgar contexts.","english_term":"tits","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"One of the most ubiquitous vulgar body-part terms in Russian; used across all adult age groups in informal settings; appears in countless memes, songs, and jokes; the root сися may relate to dialectal terms for breast or to the sucking action."}
{"term":"дойки","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"doyky","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":72,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":90,"recognition_pct_peak":90,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for female breasts derived from the verb доить (to milk a cow), directly likening a woman's breasts to a cow's udder.","english_term":"milkers","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"From доить = to milk livestock; the cow-milking metaphor is dehumanizing but the term is widely used humorously; similar register and connotation to English 'milkers' or 'udders' in crude speech."}
{"term":"буфера","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"bufera","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":48,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang for female breasts, literally 'buffers' (as in train bumpers or mechanical shock absorbers), playing on the protrusion and cushioning of large breasts.","english_term":"bumpers","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Буфер = buffer/bumper (mechanical/railway); the plural буфера evokes locomotive front buffers; humorous in tone rather than purely derogatory; comparable to English 'knockers' or 'bumpers.'"}
{"term":"цицки","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"tsitski","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":65,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":82,"recognition_pct_peak":82,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Crude slang for female breasts; phonetically similar to сиськи but phonologically distinct; common in southern Russian dialects, Ukrainian-influenced speech, and informal internet usage.","english_term":"tits","english_translation_quality":"direct","notes":"Possibly derived from or reinforced by Ukrainian цицьки; in contemporary Russian internet culture often used interchangeably with сиськи; the phonetic form suggests dialectal or cross-Slavic origin."}
{"term":"арбузы","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"arbuzy","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":42,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":80,"recognition_pct_peak":80,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Humorous slang for large female breasts, literally 'watermelons'; emphasizes size and roundness rather than being derogatory.","english_term":"melons","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Used specifically to imply large breasts; the watermelon metaphor parallels English 'melons'; tone is more admiring or humorous than degrading; арбуз is also simply the everyday Russian word for watermelon."}
{"term":"шары","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"shary","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_crude","crude":55,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":58,"recognition_pct_peak":58,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Slang for female breasts meaning 'balls' or 'spheres'; less reliable in this sense than other breast terms because шары more commonly refers to eyes or testicles in standard Russian slang.","english_term":"orbs","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Шары primarily means 'eyes' in criminal argot and 'testicles' in general crude slang; its use for 'breasts' is contextually dependent and less universal than сиськи or дойки; may cause ambiguity without clear context."}
{"term":"сиси","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"sisi","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"euphemism","crude":18,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":88,"recognition_pct_peak":88,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Childish or playful euphemism for female breasts; softer than сиськи; used when talking to young children, in affectionate contexts, or when playfully avoiding more explicit terms.","english_term":"titties","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Likely a reduplication or softened form related to the сиська root; the infantilizing form substantially lowers crudeness; used by adults in tender or playful registers as well as with children."}
{"term":"кабачки","lang":"ru","script":"cyrl","romanization":"kabachki","category":"organs","subcategory":"breast","concept":"breasts","is_novel_concept":false,"register":"slang_neutral","crude":38,"technical":5,"recognition_pct_current":45,"recognition_pct_peak":45,"peak_year":null,"regional":null,"definition":"Humorous slang for female breasts, literally 'zucchinis' or 'courgettes'; implies an elongated or somewhat pendulous shape rather than round fullness.","english_term":"zucchinis","english_translation_quality":"approximate","notes":"Кабачок = zucchini/courgette; the vegetable metaphor implies a specific elongated shape and is less flattering than арбузы; used mostly in humorous or self-deprecating contexts; awareness as a breast term is lower than арбузы or сиськи."}
